  "title": "new vs Object.create",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Two ways to set the prototype\n\n`new Fn()` runs `Fn` and sets the instance proto to `Fn.prototype`.\n\n`Object.create(proto)` makes an object whose proto is `proto` and does not run a constructor. Use `create` when you want a chain without `new`."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "create-null",
      "promptMd": "`Object.create(null)` has…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "object-proto",
          "md": "`Object.prototype` as its proto"
        },
        {
          "id": "null-proto",
          "md": "No prototype — a clean dictionary"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "null-proto"
    },
    {
